Good afternoon,

We are instructed to notify an impact by vehicle at our client's Kestrel Ridge Retail Center. Our reference is HV/RET/2025/9083.

A caution on the policy number quoted below. It has been taken from the property manager's certificate binder and it does not resolve on our own system either. Please search on the property address and our reference - we think a digit is out of order and we are checking the schedule.

Policy number as recorded in the binder: CP-9038-64115
Broker reference: HV/RET/2025/9083
Insured name: Kestrel Ridge Holdings, LP
Managing agent: Aspenwall Commercial Realty, LLC
Date of loss: 6 November 2025
Loss location: 4840 North Eagle Ridge Boulevard, Boise, ID 83713
Cause: Impact by vehicle - pickup through the anchor storefront
Estimated loss: USD 408,500

A pickup accelerated across four parking rows on Thursday morning and went
through the anchor storefront, coming to rest about eleven feet inside the sales
floor. The driver is 78 and the police report suggests a medical event; there is
no suggestion of impairment and no citation as at the report date.

The impact took out a storefront mullion that our engineer says is a bearing
element for the entry canopy. The canopy is shored and the entrance is re-routed.
A tenant employee was cut by flying glass and treated and released.

The anchor tenant is closed and is compiling their own claim; their improvements
were installed at their expense under the lease so we have pointed them at their
own carrier. The driver's insurer is Ridgeline Mutual and we assume you will pursue.

Attached:

  * the completed loss notice
  * structural assessment
  * reinstatement schedule

Please confirm a claim reference and an adjuster, and confirm that the reduced
vehicle impact deductible applies rather than the all other perils figure. We also
need retrospective approval for shoring at USD 21,400 against the USD 15,000
allowance.

